<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction - Sept 24.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction - Sept 24.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	23.28	    - 10	    22.88     23.95</p>
<p>91-Day	26.75	    - 55	    26.49     26.88</p>
<p>181-Day     28.16	    - 52	    27.99     28.39</p>
<p>343-Day     28.03				27.96     28.07</p>
<p>Last week the 350-day paper was assigned at 29.18 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   3.18 bln pesos     3.53</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   4.71 bln pesos     5.23</p>
<p>181-Day     900 million pesos   4.66 bln pesos     5.18</p>
<p>343-Day     600 million pesos   2.92 bln pesos     4.87</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.69 compared with 3.32 the week before, on total demand this week of 15.48 billion pesos.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   67 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   13 basis points</p>
<p>    181-Day			  23 basis points</p>
<p>    343-Day			   4 basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559. E-mail at robert.kozak@reuters.com</p>
